info.description:
Seeker & Solver app endpoints of Synap Mentor, generated from `docs/api-endpoints.json`.

- Request/response **shapes are traced from the Go source**; example values are placeholders built from each field's type (uuid -> `01a0fd59-0000-7000-8000-000000000000`, date-time -> `2026-10-02T10:00:00Z`, enums -> first allowed value). Each request's description holds the exact field types, validation, errors and the live-check result.
- Static: every request/response shape re-traced from the current Go source on 2026-10-06 (routes.go / cmd/main.go -> handler -> service/repository -> domain types). Dynamic (2026-10-06): all GET endpoints called against the running dev API at :8081 as anonymous, a fresh seeker and a fresh solver (email-verified, standard KYC, complete profile, pseudo name set). Each endpoint's `live_check` records the calls, statuses and whether the live body matched the documented shape. State-changing endpoints (POST/PUT/PATCH/DELETE) were not called. Content detail/stream/body were called anonymously only, because a signed-in first view writes content_views and credits the creator.

**Getting started**
1. Set `baseUrl` (default `http://127.0.0.1:8081`).
2. Run `Seeker App > Auth > POST /auth/login` (same endpoint for seeker and solver accounts). The API sets the `access_token` cookie, which Postman's cookie jar sends automatically. When the API runs with ENVIRONMENT=development and SHOW_TOKENS_IN_RESPONSE=true the token is also in the body and the test script stores it in `accessToken` (sent as Bearer).
3. Run any GET once - the collection test script stores the `csrf_token` cookie into `csrfToken`, sent as `X-CSRF-Token` on writes.
4. Sessions are bound to client identity (User-Agent/IP): keep using the same Postman client after login.
5. Every request sends `X-App-Platform: {{appPlatform}}`, `X-App-Version: {{appVersion}}` and `X-Timezone: {{timezone}}` (defaults web / 1.0.0 / UTC). Outside ENVIRONMENT=development/testing the first two are required. To test as the mobile app, set `appPlatform` to `ios` or `android`: login/verify-otp/recover-account then return `access_token` + `refresh_token` in the body (saved automatically, sent as Bearer), no cookies are set, refresh/logout take `refresh_token` in the JSON body, and writes need no CSRF token as long as no auth cookies are sent.

**Common rules and responses (not repeated per request)**
```json
{
  "client_headers": {
    "X-App-Platform": {
      "required_when": "CLIENT_REQUIRE_HEADERS=true (code default true; key not present in Backend/.env, so true) AND ENVIRONMENT is not 'development'/'testing'. In ENVIRONMENT=development or testing a missing value is defaulted to 'web' before the required check, so it can never be reported missing there (Backend/.env: ENVIRONMENT=development).",
      "allowed_values": "ios | android | web (value is trimmed and lower-cased first, so 'iOS' is accepted)",
      "length_limit": "none checked",
      "default_when_missing": "development/testing: 'web' (ClientContext locals only). Other environments with CLIENT_REQUIRE_HEADERS=false: no default - middleware passes through without validating anything else or setting client locals.",
      "effects": [
        "Validated by ClientContextMiddleware; stored in Locals client_platform / client_metadata (no handler reads these locals).",
        "Native mode is decided separately by middleware.IsNativeClient, which reads the RAW header (trim + lower-case) and returns true only for ios|android; the dev default 'web' does not affect it.",
        "ios|android: AuthMiddleware / OptionalAuthMiddleware accept 'Authorization: Bearer' even when ENVIRONMENT=production.",
        "ios|android: CSRFProtection skips the check when no access_token/refresh_token cookie is sent (no Authorization header needed).",
        "ios|android: POST /auth/login, /auth/verify-otp, /auth/verify-magic-link, /auth/recover-account return tokens in the JSON body and set no auth cookies; POST /auth/refresh does so only when the refresh token came from the body.",
        "Selects the per-platform minimum version for the 426 check (CLIENT_MIN_IOS_VERSION / CLIENT_MIN_ANDROID_VERSION / CLIENT_MIN_WEB_VERSION)."
      ]
    },
    "X-App-Version": {
      "required_when": "Same rule as X-App-Platform (CLIENT_REQUIRE_HEADERS=true and ENVIRONMENT not development/testing). development/testing default it to '1.0.0'.",
      "format": "semantic version 'major.minor.patch': exactly three dot-separated parts, each parsed with strconv.Atoi (so integers; no pre-release/build suffix). Trimmed.",
      "length_limit": "max 32 characters (checked first, in every environment, even when headers are optional)",
      "default_when_missing": "development/testing: '1.0.0'. Otherwise (headers optional) no default: missing version -> pass-through with no validation.",
      "effects": [
        "Stored in Locals client_version / client_metadata; drives CapabilityResolver.ResolveCapabilities -> Locals client_capabilities (no handler reads these).",
        "Compared to the platform minimum when CLIENT_ENFORCE_VERSION_CHECKS=true (code default false; not in Backend/.env, so OFF): lower -> 426. Minimums default '1.0.0' each; a blank/unparseable configured minimum disables the floor (fail-open)."
      ]
    },
    "X-Timezone": {
      "required_when": "never required (comment at client_context.go:135-137).",
      "format": "IANA zone name accepted by time.LoadLocation (e.g. 'Asia/Kolkata', 'UTC'); results cached. Trimmed.",
      "length_limit": "max 64 characters (checked first, in every environment)",
      "default_when_missing": "'UTC'",
      "validation_scope": "Only validated when platform AND version are both present (or defaulted in development/testing); if headers are optional and platform/version are missing, an invalid X-Timezone is not checked.",
      "effects": [
        "Stored in Locals client_timezone (unused by handlers).",
        "Separately read (not via the middleware) by TimezoneMiddleware as informational Locals browser_timezone, and by solver availability handlers as a fallback timezone when the request body has none (ValidateIANATimezone: no '/' -> 'UTC')."
      ]
    },
    "User-Agent": {
      "required_when": "Same rule as X-App-Platform (CLIENT_REQUIRE_HEADERS=true and ENVIRONMENT not development/testing). development/testing default it to 'SynapMentor-Dev/1.0' (middleware locals only).",
      "length_limit": "truncated to 500 bytes for client_metadata only; never rejected for length",
      "default_when_missing": "development/testing: 'SynapMentor-Dev/1.0' inside client_metadata only. Handlers read c.Get('User-Agent') themselves (raw, untruncated, no default) when recording user_sessions / login_attempts / eula_acceptances / logout_events.",
      "effects": [
        "Stored in Locals client_metadata.UserAgent."
      ]
    },
    "config": {
      "CLIENT_REQUIRE_HEADERS": "bool, default true (config.go:627); not set in Backend/.env",
      "CLIENT_ENFORCE_VERSION_CHECKS": "bool, default false (config.go:628); not set in Backend/.env",
      "CLIENT_MIN_IOS_VERSION / CLIENT_MIN_ANDROID_VERSION / CLIENT_MIN_WEB_VERSION": "string, default '1.0.0' each (config.go:629-631); not set in Backend/.env",
      "ENVIRONMENT": "default 'development' (config.go:470); Backend/.env:4 sets 'development'. ClientContextMiddleware reads os.Getenv('ENVIRONMENT') directly; 'development' and 'testing' both make headers optional/defaulted.",
      "getEnvAsBool": "strconv.ParseBool; unparseable value -> default (config.go:915-922)"
    },
    "net_effect_in_current_dev_env": "ENVIRONMENT=development: missing X-App-Platform / X-App-Version / User-Agent are defaulted, so no 'Missing required header' errors; supplied values are still validated (invalid platform, non-semver version, bad timezone, over-long version/timezone -> 400). Version enforcement off, so no 426."
  },
  "client_header_errors": [
    {
      "status": 400,
      "body": {
        "success": false,
        "error": "X-Timezone header value too long",
        "meta": {
          "timestamp": "string<date-time> (RFC3339)",
          "request_id": "string"
        }
      },
      "when": "X-Timezone (trimmed) longer than 64 chars - any environment, checked first"
    },
    {
      "status": 400,
      "body": {
        "success": false,
        "error": "X-App-Version header value too long",
        "meta": {
          "timestamp": "string<date-time>",
          "request_id": "string"
        }
      },
      "when": "X-App-Version (trimmed) longer than 32 chars - any environment"
    },
    {
      "status": 400,
      "body": {
        "success": false,
        "error": "Missing required header: X-App-Platform",
        "meta": {
          "timestamp": "string<date-time>",
          "request_id": "string"
        }
      },
      "when": "CLIENT_REQUIRE_HEADERS=true, ENVIRONMENT not development/testing, header empty"
    },
    {
      "status": 400,
      "body": {
        "success": false,
        "error": "Missing required header: X-App-Version",
        "meta": {
          "timestamp": "string<date-time>",
          "request_id": "string"
        }
      },
      "when": "as above, X-App-Version empty"
    },
    {
      "status": 400,
      "body": {
        "success": false,
        "error": "Missing required header: User-Agent",
        "meta": {
          "timestamp": "string<date-time>",
          "request_id": "string"
        }
      },
      "when": "as above, User-Agent empty"
    },
    {
      "status": 400,
      "body": {
        "success": false,
        "error": "Invalid X-App-Platform header. Must be one of: ios, android, web",
        "meta": {
          "timestamp": "string<date-time>",
          "request_id": "string"
        }
      },
      "when": "platform and version both present (or defaulted) and platform not ios|android|web"
    },
    {
      "status": 400,
      "body": {
        "success": false,
        "error": "Invalid X-App-Version header. Must be in semantic version format (e.g., 1.2.3)",
        "meta": {
          "timestamp": "string<date-time>",
          "request_id": "string",
          "details": "string (parser error, e.g. 'invalid semantic version format: 1.2 (expected: major.minor.patch)' / 'invalid major version: x')"
        }
      },
      "when": "platform valid, version not three integer parts"
    },
    {
      "status": 426,
      "body": {
        "success": false,
        "error": "Your app version is no longer supported. Please update to continue.",
        "meta": {
          "timestamp": "string<date-time>",
          "request_id": "string",
          "current_version": "string (normalised major.minor.patch)",
          "minimum_version": "string",
          "platform": "string enum: ios|android|web",
          "upgrade_required": true
        }
      },
      "when": "CLIENT_ENFORCE_VERSION_CHECKS=true (default false) and version < the configured minimum for that platform (minimum blank/unparseable -> no check)"
    },
    {
      "status": 400,
      "body": {
        "success": false,
        "error": "Invalid X-Timezone header. Must be in IANA timezone format (e.g., America/New_York, UTC)",
        "meta": {
          "timestamp": "string<date-time>",
          "request_id": "string"
        }
      },
      "when": "X-Timezone supplied, platform+version present, and time.LoadLocation rejects it"
    }
  ],
  "auth": "AuthMiddleware (auth.go:120-214): token = access_token cookie (always tried first, every environment). Only if the cookie is empty, 'Authorization: Bearer <token>' is used when the environment passed in (cfg.Server.Environment; middleware defaults to 'development' when empty) is not exactly 'production', OR when X-App-Platform is ios|android (IsNativeClient). So in production browsers are cookie-only and the native app is Bearer; any other environment value (development, testing, staging...) accepts Bearer from anyone. A present-but-invalid cookie is not retried with the Bearer header. Bearer parsing: header split on single spaces into exactly 2 parts with part[0]=='Bearer' (BearerToken, native_client.go:26-31). Then PASETO verify (purpose/audience 'access') -> revoked_sessions check -> user_sessions active + DB role. 401 bodies unchanged: 'Authentication required' / 'Invalid or expired token' / 'Session has been revoked. Please login again' / 'Session has been revoked or client identity mismatch. Please login again'. OptionalAuthMiddleware (auth.go:235-295) uses the same cookie-then-Bearer rule (same environment/native condition) but every failure falls through anonymously instead of 401. Per-route middleware passed in Fiber v3's 2nd positional slot still never runs (the 2nd argument is the handler, the variadic tail runs first). Since 2026-10-09 21:10 /auth/logout passes OptionalAuthMiddleware and /auth/ws-token passes AuthMiddleware in the variadic tail (routes.go:137-138, 153-156), so both now run before their handlers; Logout additionally answers 401 'Authentication required' (with meta) when OptionalAuthMiddleware identified nobody and no session was revoked (user_auth_handler.go:1499-1553).",
  "native_clients": {
    "detection": "X-App-Platform header, trimmed + lower-cased, equal to 'ios' or 'android' (IsNativeClient, native_client.go:16-22). Client-supplied; only changes how tokens travel, every request still needs a valid PASETO token + active session.",
    "tokens_in_body_no_cookies": [
      "POST /api/v1/auth/login (user_auth_handler.go:539-559)",
      "POST /api/v1/auth/verify-otp (user_auth_handler.go:923-943)",
      "POST /api/v1/auth/verify-magic-link (user_auth_handler.go:1126-1141; since 2026-10-09 21:10)",
      "POST /api/v1/auth/recover-account (user_auth_handler.go:1671-1689)",
      "POST /api/v1/auth/refresh - only when the refresh token was read from the JSON body (no refresh_token cookie) AND native (user_auth_handler.go:1175-1188, 1228-1250); body = RefreshTokenResponse {access_token, refresh_token, expires_in, refresh_token_expires_in, token_type}"
    ],
    "body_shape": "Login-type endpoints return the raw domain.LoginResponse {access_token, refresh_token, user_id, role, access_token_expires_in, refresh_token_expires_in, expires_in, token_type, remember_me_duration} (omitempty tags; mfa_* never set). tokensInBody(native) = native || (ENVIRONMENT=='development' && SHOW_TOKENS_IN_RESPONSE=='true') (user_auth_handler.go:32-34).",
    "not_native_aware": "Only Login, VerifyOTP, VerifyMagicLink, RecoverAccount and RefreshToken call IsNativeClient (user_auth_handler.go:539,923,1126,1188,1671), besides AuthMiddleware/OptionalAuthMiddleware (auth.go:146,248) and CSRFProtection (csrf.go:113). Logout, admin auth (/auth/admin/*), OAuth and all other handlers do not; their responses are identical for native and web (Logout always sends the cookie-clearing Set-Cookie headers). For browsers VerifyMagicLink now mirrors Login: SecureLoginResponse + cookies, or raw tokens + cookies when ENVIRONMENT=development and SHOW_TOKENS_IN_RESPONSE=true (user_auth_handler.go:1132-1158).",
    "refresh": "Native app sends {\"refresh_token\": \"...\"} in the JSON body with X-App-Platform ios|android and no refresh_token cookie. /auth/refresh is CSRF-exempt by path. If a refresh_token cookie is present it wins and the web (cookie) response is returned even with a native header. On failure the cookie-clearing Set-Cookie headers are still sent.",
    "logout": "POST /api/v1/auth/logout runs OptionalAuthMiddleware (routes.go:137-138). Refresh token from cookie else JSON body 'refresh_token'; access token from cookie else 'Authorization: Bearer' (handler-level, any environment). Native logout = body refresh_token (+ optional Bearer access token, which also identifies the caller to OptionalAuthMiddleware in production because the request is native); CSRF is skipped for it (no auth cookies). 200 when the caller was authenticated or at least one live session was revoked; otherwise 401 'Authentication required'. A refresh token of an already-revoked or expired session no longer counts (user_login_service.go:647-651). Response is the same for all clients and always carries cookie-clearing Set-Cookie headers (also on the 401).",
    "csrf_skip": "Non-safe methods skip CSRF when IsNativeClient AND no access_token cookie AND no refresh_token cookie (csrf.go:113). No Authorization header is needed (changed 2026-10-09 21:10; before, a non-empty Bearer header was also required and any junk Bearer string satisfied it on public routes). So every logged-out native call (request-otp, verify-otp, request-magic-link, verify-magic-link, reset-password*, resend-verification, recover-account) works without a CSRF token, and Bearer calls on authenticated routes are still verified by AuthMiddleware (bad token -> 401, not 403). Sending any auth cookie puts the request back under the double-submit check."
  },
  "auth_errors": [
    {
      "status": 401,
      "body": {
        "success": false,
        "error": "Authentication required"
      }
    },
    {
      "status": 401,
      "body": {
        "success": false,
        "error": "Invalid or expired token"
      }
    },
    {
      "status": 401,
      "body": {
        "success": false,
        "error": "Session has been revoked. Please login again"
      }
    },
    {
      "status": 401,
      "body": {
        "success": false,
        "error": "Session has been revoked or client identity mismatch. Please login again"
      }
    },
    {
      "status": 403,
      "body": {
        "success": false,
        "error": "You do not have permission to access this resource"
      },
      "when": "role check (RequireRole) fails"
    }
  ],
  "csrf": {
    "rule": "CSRFProtection(cfg.Server.Environment) is global (main.go:3282) and runs after CORS, before ClientContext. isProduction := environment != 'development' (so 'testing' is treated as production here). GET/HEAD/OPTIONS: pass; a GET without a csrf_token cookie gets one seeded (64 hex chars, Max-Age 86400, Path /, Domain $COOKIE_DOMAIN, not HttpOnly, Secure=isProduction, SameSite Strict in production else Lax). Other methods are exempt when c.Path() CONTAINS any of: '/auth/login', '/auth/admin/login', '/auth/admin/refresh', '/auth/register', '/auth/refresh', '/auth/verify-email', '/auth/forgot-password', '/auth/oauth/', '/webhooks/' (substring match, so '/auth/register-seeker' and '/auth/verify-email-seeker' are exempt too). Next, native skip (csrf.go:113-115): X-App-Platform ios|android (IsNativeClient) + no access_token and no refresh_token cookie -> pass. No Authorization header is required (since 2026-10-09 21:10; before, a non-empty Bearer header was also needed); any auth cookie keeps the request under the double-submit check. Next, development only (environment exactly 'development'): header X-CSRF-Token equal (constant-time) to env CSRF_STATIC_TOKEN -> pass (Backend/.env:5 sets it; ignored in every other environment). Otherwise header X-CSRF-Token must be non-empty and equal (constant-time) to the csrf_token cookie, in all environments.",
    "errors": [
      {
        "status": 403,
        "body": {
          "success": false,
          "error": "CSRF token missing"
        },
        "when": "csrf_token cookie or X-CSRF-Token header empty (no meta key)"
      },
      {
        "status": 403,
        "body": {
          "success": false,
          "error": "CSRF token mismatch"
        },
        "when": "header != cookie (no meta key)"
      }
    ]
  },
  "cors_allowed_request_headers": [
    "Origin",
    "Content-Type",
    "Accept",
    "Authorization",
    "Cache-Control",
    "Pragma",
    "X-User-Timezone",
    "X-Requested-With",
    "X-App-Platform",
    "X-App-Version",
    "X-Timezone",
    "X-Request-ID",
    "X-User-Role",
    "X-CSRF-Token",
    "X-Idempotency-Key"
  ],
  "global_error_handler": [
    {
      "status": "5xx",
      "body": {
        "success": false,
        "error": "Internal server error"
      }
    },
    {
      "status": "4xx (fiber.Error)",
      "body": {
        "success": false,
        "error": "<message>"
      }
    }
  ]
}
```

